---
import InformationLayout from '../../layouts/InformationLayout.astro';
---

<InformationLayout
  title="Privacy, plainly. — The Daily AI Pulse"
  description="How this static publication handles reader data."
  eyebrow="PRIVACY"
  heading="Privacy, plainly."
  dek="A static publication hosted on GitHub Pages, with no reader accounts or email signup form."
  current="privacy"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Reading and searching</h2>
    <p>
      Stories are delivered as static pages. Search uses a generated index in your browser; the
      publication does not run its own search server. The current site code does not include a
      publication analytics tracker.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub says that visiting a GitHub Pages site causes the visitor’s IP address to be logged for
      security purposes. See{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection">
        GitHub Pages data collection
      </a>{' '}
      and{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement">
        GitHub’s privacy statement
      </a>{' '}
      for its practices.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      Following a source link, the RSS feed in a third-party reader, or a GitHub issue takes you to
      services with their own privacy practices. If email subscriptions are added, this page will
      need an update before addresses are collected.
    </p>
  </section>
</InformationLayout>

<style>
  :global(.information-page) section {
    border-top: 0;
    padding: 1.2rem 0 1.6rem;
  }
</style>
